Limit: a Buzz-route instruction already SENT whose holder is replaced before ACK is not redelivered, and a live Buzz target's 30-minute delivery window can still expire an instruction; a renewed bootstrap owner receives its predecessor's unACKed dispatch again under the same id, so consumers dedupe by message id.
Warn: in-band instructions follow one handover policy on every recovery path (runtime move, revoke, takeover, adoption, switchTo after a revoke, session stop): an actionable instruction keeps its id and goes to the next authenticated holder, and is superseded only with a recorded reason (RUN_TERMINAL, RUN_MISSING, ROLE_REPLACED, a newer escalation, a completed drain) in the same transaction; a new path that rejects instructions on its own reintroduces the loss.
