Limit: the canonical CEO notice transport requires the ACP-Hermes lane secret for its HMAC signature (CEO decision: no unsigned gateway fallback); without it notifications stay PENDING with a CEO_NOTIFICATION_ROUTE_UNAVAILABLE audit row and are delivered only once a route exists. role_room_memberships rows backfilled by v51 come from addresses current at migration time.
Warn: instructions and CEO notifications are one retained set that only an ACK or a recorded supersession ends: TTL never expires them, delivery and ACK ignore TTL for them, failed attempts never reject them, and a SENT-but-unACKed row goes back to deliverable with the same id whenever its holder or CEO target changes; any new terminal path for these kinds reintroduces loss.
