Limit: the v51 membership backfill trusts v50's rule that every non-null address change is audited (connect, reattach and canonical correction audit; disconnect sets null), so later generations without an address audit inherit their room from the last proven one; an unaudited in-place change or a room change without an address audit makes the migration refuse, naming the roles, and roll back.
Warn: only a failure recorded as repairable (the target had no room or identity) is re-armed, and only for rows addressed to the holder whose route changed; authority, wrong-target, security and terminal failures are never reactivated by a route change, and a Buzz send with an unknown outcome is never re-sent to the same receiver because Buzz has no same-id dedupe or receipt.
