Limit: receiver equality for a handed-over send is judged only from outbox_sent_destinations (room, recipient key, ACCEPTED/UNKNOWN) recorded at send time; a crash between the relay accepting a send and its ACCEPTED record leaves no evidence, so the claim lease expires and the row is sent again (at-least-once).
Warn: v51 records no historical room membership: each active role's room is known only from max(binding creation, recorded runtime move, session.updated_at), which holds because every writer of sessions.buzz_address sets updated_at in the same statement (a test pins the writer set); mail signed before that is refused with a durable SIGNED_BEFORE_KNOWN_ROOM_HISTORY record and never replayed on inferred authority. A new address writer that does not stamp updated_at breaks the anchor.
