Limit: Buzz signs whole seconds, so the membership floor is known-since rounded up to the next whole second; and a handover plus a fresh send to the same destination while the first send is still pending can duplicate the message (a duplicate, not a loss).
Warn: a v51 anchor needs the latest recorded runtime move (including a return to the binding's own session) to land on the current runtime, or, with no move record, the current runtime to be the binding's own session; otherwise the role is a RUNTIME_MOVE_UNRECORDED fallback anchored at migration time, listed by migration-plan's v51AnchorFallback, and a deploy must refuse while that list is non-empty because its stop-window mail would be refused.
